        "name": "AlexxKay",
        "username": "AlexxKay",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/59ef9b/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-11-28T07:10:03.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I'm playing against the Dreamer, who has been flipped.&nbsp; A Treacherous Ape (or Illusory Demon) is in play.&nbsp; I do enough damage to kill it.</p><p>There are now two effects that seem to be happening \"at the same time\":</p><p>Dreamer:\n\n\n<span>Whenever a Projection card is destroyed, put it under this card. </span></p><p>TA:\n\n\n<span>When this card is destroyed, destroy 1 Equipment card.</span></p><p>I see two models of interpreting what happens here that seem reasonable (and I may have missed others)</p><p>1) Cards always do their own \"on destruction\" effects before other \"on destruction\" effects happen.&nbsp; So the TA destroys an equpment card, then gets put under Dreamer.</p><p>2) Since the timing is ambiguous, players choose.&nbsp; If the players choose to trigger Dreamer's effect first, the TA will no longer have any text on it (due to being under Dreamer), so no equipment card will be destroyed.</p><p>Thoughts?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:42:55.819Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
