        "raw": "<p>I&#39;m playing against the Dreamer, who has been flipped.&nbsp; A Treacherous Ape (or Illusory Demon) is in play.&nbsp; I do enough damage to kill it.</p><p>There are now two effects that seem to be happening &quot;at the same time&quot;:</p><p>Dreamer:\r\n<style type=\"text/css\">\r\n<!--td {border: 1px solid #ccc;}br {mso-data-placement:same-cell;}--></style>\r\n<span style=\"font-size:13px;font-family:calibri,arial,sans,sans-serif;color:#000000;text-align:left;\">Whenever a Projection card is destroyed, put it under this card. </span></p><p>TA:\r\n<style type=\"text/css\">\r\n<!--td {border: 1px solid #ccc;}br {mso-data-placement:same-cell;}--></style>\r\n<span style=\"font-size:110.0%;font-family:calibri,arial,sans,sans-serif;color:#000000;text-align:left;\">When this card is destroyed, destroy 1 Equipment card.</span></p><p>I see two models of interpreting what happens here that seem reasonable (and I may have missed others)</p><p>1) Cards always do their own &quot;on destruction&quot; effects before other &quot;on destruction&quot; effects happen.&nbsp; So the TA destroys an equpment card, then gets put under Dreamer.</p><p>2) Since the timing is ambiguous, players choose.&nbsp; If the players choose to trigger Dreamer&#39;s effect first, the TA will no longer have any text on it (due to being under Dreamer), so no equipment card will be destroyed.</p><p>Thoughts?</p>",
