        "raw": "<p>&quot;When this card is destroyed&quot; basically pauses the destruction process.</p><p>Time responses to destruction like &quot;When a player uses a power.&quot; &nbsp;Responses to powers trigger after the power is fully resolved, unlike &quot;When a card is played&quot; which triggers on the card entering play (and vs. one-shots the response effectively goes first)</p><p>So responses to destruction should come after the &quot;When this card is destroyed&quot; text resolves.</p><p>Cards without that text can have their effects interupted by destruction, but destruction starts, the &quot;When destroyed&quot; text occurs (and cannot be stopped) then after that text resolves responses to the destruction take place.</p><p>So TA will destroy an equipment before leaving play, then it leaves play and destruction responses activate.</p><p>This process can be wholly circumnavigated by any card that says &quot;when a card would be destroyed do something else&nbsp;<strong>instead</strong>&quot; &nbsp;Like in Final Wasteland. &nbsp;A card that fits the criteria (destroyed by env. damage for the one in final wasteland) it is not treated as destroyed, and none of the destruction effects will trigger.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Various rulings are referenced here, but putting it together into a sensible order just how I deduce it. &nbsp;Some of those rulings:</p><p>1. &nbsp;&quot;When a card enters play&quot; triggers when the card enters play.</p><p>1a. Informant cannot have her effect prevented by a one shot that would destroy her.</p><p>2. &nbsp;On destruct effects do not trigger when Unforgiving Wasteland text criteria is met, the card is removed from play and not destroyed.</p><p>3. &nbsp;&quot;When a Power is used&quot; reaction comes after the power resolves.</p>",
